// Two NPCs the fixture map can spawn, and the only thing they are for is the
// moment they are created.
//
// A MAP'S OWN NPC IS SPAWNED BEFORE CGAME EXISTS, and that is the whole point.
// G_SetG2PlayerModel asks for its skin while the level spawns, so the name
// lands in the CS_CHARSKINS configstrings in time for the loop in
// CG_RegisterGraphics - the loop that turns configstring indexes into renderer
// handles and is the only place the two numbering spaces can be compared. The
// player cannot stand in for this: he connects AFTER cgame has initialised, his
// skin reaches the configstrings after that loop has already run, and cgs.skins
// stays empty. Measured with JKX_SMOKE_CHAR alone: not one line about skins in
// the entire engine log, and the diagnostic in that loop never fired.
//
// Two of them rather than one, because the defect is an OFFSET and one number
// cannot show a constant. Two skins registered in order say whether the gap is
// the same for both - a shift - or grows - a drift. The log from real hardware
// said shift, four, for twelve skins in a row.
//
// Everything here beyond playerModel is the minimum that makes an NPC exist and
// stand still. No weapon, so nothing spawns a saber or a blaster and no second
// Ghoul2 instance appears in the picture; TEAM_NEUTRAL and zero aggression so
// he has no reason to move, because every other check in this fixture is
// written against where the player ends up standing.

JKX
{
	playerModel	jkx
	reactions	1
	aim			1
	move		1
	aggression	1
	evasion		1
	intelligence	1
	rank		civilian
	playerTeam	TEAM_PLAYER
	enemyTeam	TEAM_ENEMY
	class		CLASS_PRISONER
	yawspeed	60
	walkSpeed	0
	runSpeed	0
	health		100
}

// The second one wears the other skin the fixture model has. Same model, so the
// only thing that differs between the two configstrings is the skin name.
JKX2
{
	playerModel	jkx
	customSkin	alt
	reactions	1
	aim			1
	move		1
	aggression	1
	evasion		1
	intelligence	1
	rank		civilian
	playerTeam	TEAM_PLAYER
	enemyTeam	TEAM_ENEMY
	class		CLASS_PRISONER
	yawspeed	60
	walkSpeed	0
	runSpeed	0
	health		100
}
